Date: Sat, 18 Jul 2026 21:39:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 094/143] drm/sun4i: sun55i_de: beam-gate on EVERY arm +
 hrtimer re-anchored to the beam (fix scanout wedge)

Root cause of the stuck frame of 2026-07-18 (wlroots direct-scanout
transitions): the retry budget (arms_left=2) left arm_pending live after every
arm, do_arm started the fallback hrtimer and vblank_quirk skipped the
beam-gated arm while the timer was active -> with sustained commits at 60fps
the hrtimer was the ONLY arm path, in open loop (line_total*ns_per_line
truncated, CLOCK_MONOTONIC vs the real PLL dotclock): the arm point drifted
across the whole frame and the AHB blocks were applied mid scanout/prefetch of
the DE. An OVL<->AFBD toggle applied mid-fetch wedges the channel config latch
(screen stuck on the old frame forever; grim/composition perfect).

Three changes, all in the same mechanism:

1. do_arm() beam-gates ALL arms: re-reads the real TCON line and defers to the
   next target if the beam left the safe window [0, line_active), capped at 3
   hops (a broken counter can only delay the chain, never stop it). It returns
   the wait lines; the timer scheduling moves to the callers.

2. Each hrtimer hop re-anchors to the beam (sun55i_de_lines_to_target over the
   real counter) instead of the blind forward of one frame; and vblank_quirk
   RECLAIMS the timer in flight (hrtimer_try_to_cancel) to become again the
   primary path anchored to the real vblank.

3. commit() starts the backstop hrtimer if none is active: the initial arm no
   longer depends 100% on the TCON vblank IRQ (if the IRQ dies, before it left
   arm_pending eternal: commits coalescing, holds not ageing and the DE
   scanning the old fb without a single error in dmesg). pr_warn at 120 commits
   without an arm to expose the stall.

New diagnostic: /sys/module/sun8i_mixer/parameters/arm_gated.
